WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.880
If you watch the next 20 minutes, you'll know Claude better than 90% of the population.

2
00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:07.280
Most people use Claude like regular Google.

3
00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.840
They ask questions, and that's where the story ends.

4
00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:13.780
It's like buying an ultra-sport car and driving it to the store.

5
00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:15.140
It just makes no sense.

6
00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:19.420
That's why in this quick mini-course I'll show you how to get the most out of Claude

7
00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:21.620
and put it to work today.

8
00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:23.360
Why use Claude at all?

9
00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:27.560
The point is not to ask questions but to let Claude work for you.

10
00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.520
And it can do all sorts of things for you.

11
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.320
That is, you connect it to your computer, give it access and let it work.

12
00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:36.660
So we don't waste time, let's go straight to practice.

13
00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:38.660
If you're afraid Claude doesn't know anything about you,

14
00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:42.660
and you've already left a lot of information in ChatGPT or another AI model,

15
00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:44.700
let's transfer that to Claude.

16
00:00:44.840 --> 00:00:48.600
We open Claude in the browser and get to the import option.

17
00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:52.160
We get a question that we'll copy into ChatGPT.

18
00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:56.440
The answers we got from ChatGPT we bring back into Claude

19
00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:00.940
and now Claude has the information that ChatGPT has about us.

20
00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:03.180
The second step — we choose the best model.

21
00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:07.220
If you use the free version of Claude, you're limited in your choice of models.

22
00:01:07.620 --> 00:01:14.600
Claude adds new things literally every week, and right now the strongest of the existing models is Fable 5.

23
00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:16.740
That means it spends the most credits.

24
00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:19.340
Since we've mentioned credits, what are credits?

25
00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:24.080
Every Claude plan, whether free, $20, 100 or 200,

26
00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:26.960
has a certain number of credits that can be used.

27
00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:32.340
Every request you give Claude, or action you assign it, spends a certain number of credits.

28
00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:35.640
And this spending depends on how powerful the model you use is

29
00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:37.880
and how complex the task is.

30
00:01:38.040 --> 00:01:40.680
That is, if you ask an ordinary question, fewer credits are spent.

31
00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:45.300
If you turn on Fable 5, the strongest model, at maximum power

32
00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:49.020
and tell it to build an app, it will burn through credits quickly.

33
00:01:49.180 --> 00:01:52.160
Unless you're on a more expensive plan at $100 or $200.

34
00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:55.580
My advice is always this: start with the $20 plan.

35
00:01:55.820 --> 00:01:58.680
The free one has the worst possible models.

36
00:01:58.860 --> 00:02:01.980
Only when on the $20 plan you start hitting limits,

37
00:02:02.480 --> 00:02:05.740
when they tell you to wait 5 hours, wait a few days,

38
00:02:05.980 --> 00:02:08.420
then it's time to buy the most expensive plan.

39
00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:12.920
Use Haiku 4.5 for tasks that don't require much brains,

40
00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:15.560
working with spreadsheets, anything simpler.

41
00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:19.600
Use Sonnet 5 for everyday things.

42
00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:29.600
For more complex tasks there's Opus 5, which came out recently: in some ways it's almost as good as Fable 5, and in some ways better, and it spends fewer credits.

43
00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:34.360
And use Fable 5 for the most complex tasks.

44
00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:43.020
When you choose a model, you also have its strength — that's "effort," and depending on the complexity of the task you choose what that effort is.

45
00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:48.040
The lowest, of course, spends the fewest credits, and the maximum spends ultra many credits.

46
00:02:48.040 --> 00:02:55.120
And when you choose Fable 5 and set the effort to maximum, it will eat all your credits, so use it carefully.

47
00:02:55.480 --> 00:03:02.280
A skill that will matter more and more is knowing which model to use in which situation, because credits aren't infinite.

48
00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:06.300
The third point — connectors, the best thing in Claude.

49
00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:11.460
What do connectors do? You literally link your Claude with all possible apps.

50
00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:19.900
What does it look like in practice? You connect Claude to Gmail. It reads all your emails, analyzes them, replies to emails, puts them in drafts.

51
00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:27.620
You connect it to Facebook ad campaigns. It analyzes all your campaigns, can launch them directly, and from the chat it can launch campaigns.

52
00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:31.440
Now I'll show you my connectors. Here I have around a dozen connectors.

53
00:03:31.440 --> 00:03:42.320
Canva, Circle, Facebook ads, Gmail, Google Drive, Higgsfield for creating videos and photos, HubSpot, MailerLite, SEMrush and many other plugins.

54
00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:46.440
I don't need to go into these apps directly at all, I can control them from Claude.

55
00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:54.240
Here's a great example: HubSpot, a CRM where all customer data lives, and you need to add a new order to every customer.

56
00:03:54.400 --> 00:03:58.660
That is, a thousand some orders, if done manually, would take forever.

57
00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:04.660
Through Claude you connect HubSpot and in literally half an hour Claude does this work for you.

58
00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:06.820
The fourth point — Claude artifacts.

59
00:04:06.960 --> 00:04:09.080
Mini-apps inside your Claude.

60
00:04:09.080 --> 00:04:15.080
You have various spreadsheets filled with different data, and you want it to look nice visually, as if someone had programmed it for you.

61
00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:18.540
In a Claude artifact you can have such an app.

62
00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:26.080
You connect a spreadsheet that data flows into, and literally every day you can come in and look at an interactive view of this data.

63
00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:30.340
This is an example of an artifact in which a customer database has been analyzed.

64
00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:32.480
Notice how it looks.

65
00:04:32.560 --> 00:04:38.580
This database is filled every day, this is demo data, and here you can run any analyses

66
00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:42.500
and the best part is that you can tailor it to your needs.

67
00:04:42.980 --> 00:04:45.880
If some metrics matter more to you, they can be highlighted.

68
00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:51.580
Even better, this can be shared: you click Publish and share with your team members.

69
00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:53.120
The fifth point — visualizations.

70
00:04:53.120 --> 00:05:00.260
Previously, visualizing boring data had to be done through external tools, today this is possible inside Claude.

71
00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:02.460
You paste in a table and say:

72
00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:07.060
Show me this table visually and the most important data from it.

73
00:05:07.380 --> 00:05:09.320
Look at what kind of dashboard you get.

74
00:05:09.560 --> 00:05:11.120
The sixth point — Claude projects.

75
00:05:11.320 --> 00:05:15.980
Imagine a project as a folder that you fill with all possible data for this project.

76
00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:19.300
Everything related to this project you do inside it.

77
00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:25.900
Claude uses all this data, and based on it gives you accurate information on this project, not those generic answers.

78
00:05:26.140 --> 00:05:28.480
I have projects for all areas of business.

79
00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:34.520
AI Profit Lab, finance, neuro lab, Instagram dominance, copywriting, SaaS tools.

80
00:05:34.860 --> 00:05:39.700
That is, for each project I make a separate folder and put all the valuable information into it.

81
00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:42.300
The seventh point — the Claude extension for Google Chrome.

82
00:05:43.220 --> 00:05:52.160
You connect Claude and your browser, and Claude can search, open sites, parse and do everything you can.

83
00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:54.200
That is, this saves me a lot of time.

84
00:05:54.200 --> 00:06:00.800
You look for cheap plane tickets: when you enter it directly into Claude or another tool, it'll give you data that isn't up to date.

85
00:06:01.180 --> 00:06:07.080
But this way you give it access, and it searches the way you would, sees what's current, rather than those outdated prices.

86
00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:11.680
A great example — when I was recently looking for a domain for a site, it was very hard to find one.

87
00:06:12.020 --> 00:06:16.900
However, I get 100 suggestions, and now I have to check one by one whether this domain is free.

88
00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:25.360
I launch Claude, it goes into Google Chrome and literally says: this is taken, this is free, gives an analysis, so I don't need to waste any time at all.

89
00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:28.780
The eighth point, perhaps the biggest, is Claude Cowork.

90
00:06:29.140 --> 00:06:33.480
We give Claude access to your computer, and it does what you would do.

91
00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:40.520
That is, it has access to documentation, folders, it can work, build an app, whatever you tell it, it will do.

92
00:06:40.520 --> 00:06:42.480
And this can be done remotely.

93
00:06:42.860 --> 00:06:46.360
If your computer is on, you can give a command from your phone:

94
00:06:46.720 --> 00:06:50.340
do this and that, analyze the data from such-and-such folder

95
00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:52.540
and it does all of it for you.

96
00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:56.240
On the YouTube channel "Business Stories" I have more than fifteen hundred shorts.

97
00:06:56.360 --> 00:06:58.200
Downloading them is serious work.

98
00:06:58.720 --> 00:07:01.040
Claude Cowork wrote me a Python script,

99
00:07:01.200 --> 00:07:02.680
I ran it in the background,

100
00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:05.900
it downloaded all these clips, put them in folders,

101
00:07:06.120 --> 00:07:09.900
sorted them by topic, and now I have the whole database in one place.

102
00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:17.200
The ninth point — Claude Design. You no longer need designers to make cool design for a site, presentation, anything.

103
00:07:17.420 --> 00:07:21.660
Claude Design does it for you. All you need is to give it instructions.

104
00:07:21.760 --> 00:07:28.780
I like this site, I like this style, need to do this, this and this. You run it and get a finished design.

105
00:07:28.940 --> 00:07:35.360
The way you'd communicate with a designer, you give it comments on what needs fixing, and it fixes it in the background.

106
00:07:35.360 --> 00:07:40.280
That way we can release several finished sites every week.

107
00:07:40.460 --> 00:07:46.000
If you want to use AI to earn and grow your business, join AI Profit Lab.

108
00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:51.320
There you'll find ready-made automations, ready-made systems, only what's been proven in practice.

109
00:07:51.460 --> 00:07:56.120
That is, you won't be buried in information, only what we test on real businesses,

110
00:07:56.260 --> 00:07:58.780
we publish, and you can practically just copy.

111
00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:04.240
With the coupon Vlast Digital you get almost 40% off the first month. Link in the description.

112
00:08:04.240 --> 00:08:13.060
Those were the most important points about Claude. The point is to apply at least one today, something you haven't tried before, try it in practice and see how it works for your case.

113
00:08:13.280 --> 00:08:16.200
There's no use from watching once, all this has to be applied in practice.

114
00:08:16.440 --> 00:08:19.500
If this was useful to you, give it a like, and see you in the next lesson.